insert into countries (continent, name, iso_code, flag_url, highlight_img_url, description, longdescription)
values
	('Europe', 'Iceland', 'IS', 'https://flagcdn.com/is.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1539593395743-7da5ee10ff07?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'A Nordic island nation known for its stunning natural landscapes, including glaciers, waterfalls, and geothermal activity. Iceland offers a high quality of life and excellent opportunities for nature enthusiasts.

## Key Highlights
- Stunning natural landscapes with glaciers and waterfalls
- High quality of life and excellent social services
- Unique geothermal energy and sustainable living', 'Iceland is a Nordic island nation located in the North Atlantic Ocean, known for its dramatic natural landscapes and cutting-edge approach to renewable energy. The country is famous for its spectacular waterfalls, vast glaciers, and geothermal hot springs, making it a paradise for nature lovers and adventure seekers. Reykjavik, the capital, is one of the world''s northernmost capital cities and offers a vibrant cultural scene despite its small size. Iceland has consistently ranked among the world''s highest in quality of life indices, offering excellent healthcare, education, and social services. The country has made remarkable progress in renewable energy, with geothermal and hydroelectric power providing nearly all of its electricity. For those considering relocation, Iceland offers opportunities in tech, tourism, and creative industries, though the cost of living is notably high. The Icelandic people are known for their warmth and hospitality, and English is widely spoken. The unique landscape provides year-round activities, from hiking and camping in summer to Northern Lights viewing in winter. Iceland''s strong economy and social stability make it an attractive destination for skilled workers, entrepreneurs, and families seeking a high-quality lifestyle in a sustainable society.'),
	('Europe', 'Germany', 'DE', 'https://flagcdn.com/de.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1467269204594-9661b134dd2b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'Europe''s largest economy with a strong engineering and technology sector. Germany offers excellent education, healthcare, and a rich cultural heritage spanning from Berlin to Bavaria.

## Key Highlights
- Strong economy and innovation hub
- Excellent education and healthcare systems
- Rich cultural heritage and world-class infrastructure', 'Germany is Europe''s largest economy and a global leader in engineering, automotive manufacturing, and technology innovation. With a population of over 83 million, Germany plays a central role in European politics and economics. The country is renowned for its engineering excellence, hosting world-famous companies like BMW, Mercedes-Benz, Siemens, and Deutsche Telekom. Germany''s education system is highly regarded, with numerous universities consistently ranking among the world''s best. The country offers universal healthcare, reliable public transportation, and excellent quality of life standards. Berlin, the capital, has transformed into a vibrant hub for startups and creative industries, while traditional manufacturing centers like Stuttgart and Munich remain economic powerhouses. German culture is rich and diverse, from world-class museums and classical music traditions to Oktoberfest celebrations. The country''s commitment to environmental sustainability and the "Energiewende" (energy transition) makes it a leader in renewable energy adoption. German workers benefit from strong labor rights, generous social benefits, and excellent work-life balance. The cost of living is moderate compared to other Western European countries, though major cities are increasingly expensive. For skilled professionals, Germany offers numerous opportunities in manufacturing, technology, healthcare, and finance sectors.'),
	('South America', 'Peru', 'PE', 'https://flagcdn.com/pe.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1526392060635-9d6019884377?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'Home to Machu Picchu and the Amazon rainforest, Peru is a vibrant destination with rich indigenous culture, diverse landscapes, and growing opportunities in Lima''s modern economy.

## Key Highlights
- Iconic landmarks and UNESCO World Heritage sites
- Vibrant indigenous culture and traditions
- Growing tech and business opportunities in Lima', 'Peru is a South American nation renowned for its extraordinary archaeological heritage, particularly the ancient Incan citadel of Machu Picchu, one of the world''s most iconic landmarks. The country spans three distinct geographical regions: the Pacific coastal desert, the Andes Mountains, and the Amazon rainforest, offering incredible biodiversity. Peru''s history is deeply intertwined with indigenous civilizations, and this heritage remains visible in its culture, traditions, and approximately 47 indigenous languages still spoken today. Lima, the capital, has evolved into a modern metropolis with a thriving culinary scene, recognized as one of South America''s gastronomic capitals. The country is experiencing economic growth, with Lima''s tech sector developing rapidly and attracting startup entrepreneurs. Peru offers lower costs of living compared to many developed nations while maintaining reasonable infrastructure in urban areas. The country is rich in natural resources and minerals, contributing to its economy. Expats and digital nomads are increasingly attracted to Peru for its affordable lifestyle, cultural richness, and adventure opportunities. The textile and handicraft industries are globally renowned, and tourism remains a significant economic driver. Peru''s challenges include infrastructure gaps and income inequality, but opportunities abound in tourism, education, technology, and international business sectors, particularly for Spanish-speaking professionals and entrepreneurs.'),
	('South America', 'Chile', 'CL', 'https://flagcdn.com/cl.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'A long, narrow country stretching along South America''s Pacific coast, known for the Atacama Desert, Patagonia, and the Andes. Chile offers stability and economic opportunities in South America.

## Key Highlights
- Diverse landscapes from desert to mountain to coast
- Political and economic stability in the region
- Strong opportunities in mining and technology sectors', 'Chile is one of South America''s most developed and stable nations, stretching along the continent''s western edge with an extraordinary range of landscapes. The country extends from the world''s driest desert, the Atacama, in the north to the windswept fjords and glaciers of Patagonia in the south. The Andes Mountains form the country''s eastern border, creating dramatic terrain. Santiago, the capital, is a modern cosmopolitan city with excellent infrastructure, restaurants, cultural venues, and business opportunities. Chile''s economy is relatively diversified and stable, with mining, particularly copper, remaining a major industry, but technology and renewable energy sectors rapidly expanding. The country ranks high in South America for economic development and is considered one of the region''s safest destinations. Healthcare and education standards are above regional averages, and infrastructure is relatively modern. Chile offers lower costs of living than developed nations while maintaining good services in urban areas. The country''s legal system is well-developed, making business operations relatively straightforward for foreign investors. Expats are attracted to Chile for its stability, natural beauty, and economic opportunities in tech, renewable energy, mining, and tourism sectors. The wine industry is world-renowned, offering unique opportunities. Chile''s commitment to environmental sustainability and renewable energy development presents growing opportunities. However, political changes and economic adjustments have created recent volatility.'),
	('Africa', 'Morocco', 'MA', 'https://flagcdn.com/ma.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1559586616-361e18714958?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'A North African gateway connecting Africa and Europe, featuring the Sahara Desert, Atlas Mountains, and vibrant medinas. Morocco blends ancient traditions with modern development.

## Key Highlights
- Gateway between Africa and Europe
- Rich Berber and Arab cultural heritage
- Growing tourism and trade opportunities', 'Morocco is a North African nation positioned as a bridge between Africa, Europe, and the Middle East, with a rich cultural heritage spanning Berber, Arab, and Islamic traditions. The country features diverse landscapes including the Sahara Desert, the snow-capped Atlas Mountains, and Atlantic and Mediterranean coastlines. Marrakech and Fez are known for their enchanting medinas, traditional souks, and centuries-old architecture. Rabat serves as the capital and administrative center, while Casablanca is the largest city and economic hub. Morocco''s economy is increasingly diversified, with tourism, agriculture, phosphate mining, and manufacturing as major sectors. The country is investing heavily in renewable energy, particularly solar and wind power. Marrakech and other cities are attracting international business and tech professionals. The cost of living is significantly lower than Europe, making it attractive for digital nomads and retirees. Morocco offers rich cultural experiences, beautiful beaches, desert adventures, and mountain trekking. The country is modernizing its infrastructure and internet connectivity is improving in urban areas. French and Arabic are the official languages, though Amazigh (Berber) is increasingly recognized. Morocco''s location near Europe makes it accessible while offering distinctly African and Middle Eastern experiences. Challenges include infrastructure gaps outside major cities and bureaucratic processes, but opportunities exist in tourism, renewable energy, agriculture, and creative industries. The government is working to attract foreign investment and talent.'),
	('Asia', 'Indonesia', 'ID', 'https://flagcdn.com/id.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1464822759023-fed622ff2c3b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'The world''s largest archipelago spanning thousands of islands, Indonesia offers incredible biodiversity, rich cultural heritage, and a growing economy centered around Jakarta.

## Key Highlights
- World''s largest archipelago with incredible biodiversity
- Rich and diverse cultural heritage
- Growing economy with expanding business opportunities', 'Indonesia is the world''s largest archipelago, comprising over 17,000 islands spanning three time zones across Southeast Asia. The country is incredibly diverse, with numerous ethnic groups, languages, and cultures, creating a unique blend of traditions and modern development. Java, the most populated island, is home to Jakarta, the sprawling capital city and economic center. Indonesia ranks as the world''s fourth most populous nation with over 270 million people. The country is extraordinarily biodiverse, home to a vast array of unique wildlife and plant species found nowhere else on Earth. Bali has become a major tourist destination known for its beaches, temples, and spiritual culture. Indonesia''s economy is rapidly growing, with significant opportunities in technology, e-commerce, manufacturing, and tourism sectors. The cost of living is notably low, making it attractive for digital nomads, remote workers, and expats seeking affordable living. Jakarta is developing as a tech hub with a growing startup ecosystem, though infrastructure challenges persist. Indonesia offers incredible cultural experiences, from traditional ceremonies to world-class beaches and diving. The country is investing in infrastructure improvements and digital technology. Business environment challenges include bureaucracy and corruption concerns, but opportunities abound for entrepreneurs and skilled professionals. Indonesian is the official language, and English proficiency varies. Indonesia presents an excellent balance of low costs, cultural richness, economic growth, and adventure opportunities for those seeking to live in Southeast Asia.'),
	('Europe', 'United Kingdom', 'GB', 'https://flagcdn.com/gb.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1513635269975-59663e0ac1ad?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'A major global hub for finance, culture, and education. The UK combines historical landmarks with modern innovation, offering strong opportunities in London and throughout the country.

## Key Highlights
- Global financial and cultural hub
- World-class universities and education system
- Strong opportunities in finance, tech, and creative industries', 'The United Kingdom is a major global power and economic center, comprising England, Scotland, Wales, and Northern Ireland. London is one of the world''s most important financial centers, hosting major banks, investment firms, and multinational corporations. The UK''s education system is world-renowned, home to universities like Oxford and Cambridge, consistently ranked among the world''s best. The country has a rich historical and cultural heritage, with museums, galleries, theaters, and cultural institutions of global significance. The British economy is diversified, strong in finance, professional services, creative industries, technology, healthcare, and education. London''s tech scene is rapidly growing, earning comparisons to Silicon Valley, with thriving startup ecosystems. The National Health Service (NHS) provides universal healthcare to all residents. The UK offers excellent infrastructure, reliable public transportation, and high quality of life standards. English is the official language, and immigration procedures are well-established for skilled workers. Brexit has created changes to immigration and business regulations that require careful navigation. The cost of living, particularly in London and Southeast England, is very high compared to most countries. The UK offers strong opportunities for professionals in finance, technology, healthcare, law, education, and creative fields. The country provides cultural richness, excellent universities, and access to European and global markets, though housing costs and visa requirements present challenges for prospective residents.')
on conflict (name) do nothing;

