	('Europe', 'Portugal', 'PT', 'https://flagcdn.com/pt.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1555881400-74d7acaacd8b?q=80&w=1170&auto=format&fit=crop&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxwaG90by1wYWdlfHx8fGVufDB8fHx8fA%3D%3D?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'A welcoming European nation on the Atlantic coast with a mild climate, affordable lifestyle, and rich maritime history. Portugal offers excellent wine, beaches, and a growing tech scene in Lisbon.

## Key Highlights
- Affordable cost of living with excellent lifestyle
- Beautiful beaches and mild Mediterranean climate
- Growing tech and startup ecosystem', 'Portugal is a Western European nation known for its Atlantic coastline, mild climate, and rich maritime history. Located on the Iberian Peninsula, Portugal has been a gateway to Europe for centuries. Lisbon, the capital, is increasingly recognized as a vibrant tech hub and startup destination, attracting entrepreneurs and remote workers from around the world. The cost of living is significantly lower than Northern Europe, making Portugal particularly attractive for digital nomads and those seeking affordable European living. Portuguese cuisine is underrated yet excellent, known for fresh seafood, traditional pastries, and world-class wines from the Douro Valley and other regions. The country offers beautiful beaches along both the Atlantic coast and the Algarve, as well as cultural heritage sites and charming traditional towns. Portugal has invested in renewable energy and sustainable infrastructure, ranking among Europe''s leaders in clean energy adoption. Healthcare is good and significantly cheaper than many Western countries. Portuguese is the official language, though English proficiency is increasing in urban areas and among younger people. The Portuguese are known for their warmth and welcoming nature. The government has introduced digital visa programs and startup visas to attract foreign talent and entrepreneurs. Portugal combines European stability and quality of life with affordability and a relaxed lifestyle, making it increasingly popular among expats, retirees, and remote professionals seeking a balanced lifestyle without the high costs of Northern Europe.'),
	('Europe', 'Spain', 'ES', 'https://flagcdn.com/es.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1539037116277-4db20889f2d4?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'A vibrant Mediterranean country known for its passion for life, world-class art and architecture, beautiful beaches, and delicious cuisine. Spain offers a balanced lifestyle across diverse regions.

## Key Highlights
- World-class art, architecture, and cultural heritage
- Beautiful Mediterranean beaches and coastal living
- Vibrant food culture and social lifestyle', 'Spain is a Mediterranean country renowned for its passionate culture, world-class art and architecture, and vibrant social lifestyle. Located on the Iberian Peninsula, Spain spans from Mediterranean beaches to mountain regions and interior plateaus. Madrid and Barcelona are major cities with distinct characters: Madrid is the capital and cultural center with world-class museums, while Barcelona combines modernist architecture with Mediterranean beach culture. Spain''s art heritage includes works by Goya, Velázquez, Picasso, and Dalí, housed in museums like the Prado. The country is famous for its cuisine, wine, and food culture, with Spanish gastronomy respected globally. Spain offers an excellent climate, affordable lifestyle compared to Northern Europe, and diverse landscapes. The Spanish emphasize work-life balance, with long lunch breaks and evening social time being cultural norms. Healthcare is excellent and publicly provided. Spanish is the official language, widely spoken throughout the country. Spain has experienced economic challenges but continues to attract expats, remote workers, and retirees seeking Mediterranean living. Tourism is a major industry, and many regions depend heavily on seasonal visitors. The country offers opportunities in technology, tourism, education, and creative industries, particularly in Barcelona''s tech scene and Madrid''s business environment. Spain combines Mediterranean climate, affordable living, excellent healthcare, rich culture, and vibrant social life, making it attractive for those seeking European living with relaxed Mediterranean character.'),
	('Europe', 'Estonia', 'EE', 'https://flagcdn.com/ee.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1563720786963-c3c73400d5a3?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'A Baltic tech pioneer and digital leader in Northern Europe. Estonia combines medieval charm with cutting-edge innovation and a high standard of living with affordable housing.

## Key Highlights
- World''s leading digital government and e-services
- Tech hub with affordable housing costs
- Medieval charm with modern innovation', 'Estonia is a Baltic nation that has emerged as a global leader in digital innovation and e-governance. The country has implemented one of the world''s most advanced digital infrastructures, with e-voting, e-residency programs, and digital citizenship available to residents and entrepreneurs worldwide. Tallinn, the capital, features a beautifully preserved medieval old town contrasting with modern neighborhoods. Estonia ranks among Europe''s most digitally advanced nations, making it attractive for tech entrepreneurs and IT professionals. The country offers excellent internet connectivity and has fostered a thriving startup ecosystem. Estonia''s e-residency program allows foreigners to establish and manage companies entirely online, attracting entrepreneurs globally. The cost of living is lower than Western Europe, though housing prices in Tallinn have risen due to tech industry growth. Healthcare is modern and affordable. Estonian education is highly regarded, particularly in science and mathematics. English proficiency is high among younger generations and urban professionals. The country is small (approximately 1.3 million people), creating a tight-knit society. Estonia is environmentally conscious, with extensive forests and lakes. Challenges include a smaller job market outside tech and potential language barriers for non-English speakers. Estonia combines technological innovation, affordable living, English-friendly environment, and European stability, making it particularly attractive for tech professionals, digital nomads, and entrepreneurs seeking a digitally advanced society.'),
	('Asia', 'Thailand', 'TH', 'https://flagcdn.com/th.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1552465011-b4e21bf6e79a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'The Land of Smiles offers a perfect blend of ancient temples, tropical beaches, and vibrant street food culture. Thailand''s affordable cost of living makes it attractive for digital nomads and expats.

## Key Highlights
- Extremely affordable cost of living
- Ancient temples and rich Buddhist culture
- Excellent for digital nomads and remote workers', 'Thailand is a Southeast Asian nation famous for its Buddhist temples, tropical beaches, and vibrant street food culture. Known as "The Land of Smiles," Thailand is renowned for the warmth and hospitality of its people. Bangkok, the capital, is a bustling metropolis with modern skyscrapers, ancient temples, vibrant markets, and excellent street food. The country offers extraordinary value for money, with extremely low costs for accommodation, food, transportation, and healthcare. Thailand is incredibly popular with digital nomads and remote workers who can maintain Western incomes while enjoying a tropical lifestyle. The country features diverse attractions: ancient temples in Chiang Mai, tropical island beaches, limestone karsts in Phang Nga, and mountains in the north. Thai cuisine is world-renowned, known for balancing sweet, salty, sour, and spicy flavors. Beaches like Phuket and Koh Samui attract millions of visitors annually. Healthcare is modern, affordable, and available in major cities. Thailand offers various visa options, including the Digital Nomad Visa and long-term retirement visas. English is increasingly spoken in tourist areas and among younger people, though Thai language knowledge is helpful. Challenges include visa requirements for long-term stay, potential political instability, and bureaucratic processes. The Buddhist culture shapes daily life, with temples visible throughout the country. Thailand combines affordability, natural beauty, cultural richness, and excellent infrastructure in tourist areas, making it the world''s most popular destination for digital nomads and remote workers seeking low-cost tropical living.'),
	('North America', 'Mexico', 'MX', 'https://flagcdn.com/mx.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518105779142-d975f22f1b0a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'A culturally rich nation with pre-Hispanic ruins, colonial architecture, colorful markets, and world-renowned cuisine. Mexico offers close proximity to the US and growing business opportunities.

## Key Highlights
- Rich pre-Hispanic and colonial heritage
- World-renowned cuisine and vibrant culture
- Close proximity to North America and growing economy', 'Mexico is a large North American nation with a rich cultural heritage spanning indigenous pre-Hispanic civilizations, Spanish colonial history, and modern development. The country is home to approximately 130 million people and is North America''s cultural bridge, blending indigenous and European influences. Mexico City is the capital, one of the world''s largest metropolitan areas, with museums, restaurants, and cultural venues of international importance. The country''s cuisine is UNESCO-recognized as intangible cultural heritage, celebrated globally for its complexity and regional variations. Mexico offers extremely affordable living costs, particularly outside major tourist areas, making it attractive for retirees and digital nomads. The country has extensive natural beauty: beaches on both coasts, pre-Hispanic archaeological sites, colonial cities, and diverse ecosystems. Healthcare is modern and affordable in major cities. Spanish is the official language, though English proficiency varies. Mexico''s economy is relatively large and diversified, with opportunities in tourism, manufacturing, technology, and business services. Mexico City has a growing tech scene and startup ecosystem. Proximity to the United States offers cultural and economic advantages. Mexico offers various temporary resident visas for entrepreneurs, remote workers, and retirees. Challenges include security concerns in certain regions, bureaucracy, and variable service quality outside major centers. Mexico combines cultural richness, affordability, geographic proximity to the US, economic opportunities, and natural diversity, attracting expats, retirees, and entrepreneurs seeking Latin American living with US accessibility.')
