values
	('Europe', 'United Kingdom', 'GB', 'https://flagcdn.com/gb.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1513635269975-59663e0ac1ad?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'A major global hub for finance, culture, and education. The UK combines historical landmarks with modern innovation, offering strong opportunities in London and throughout the country.

## Key Highlights
- Global financial and cultural hub
- World-class universities and education system
- Strong opportunities in finance, tech, and creative industries', 'The United Kingdom is one of the world''s most influential nations, comprising England, Scotland, Wales, and Northern Ireland. London is a global financial powerhouse hosting the London Stock Exchange and major international banks. The UK''s education system produces world-leading universities, including Oxford and Cambridge, consistently ranked among the world''s best. British culture has profoundly influenced global arts, literature, music, and entertainment. The country boasts exceptional museums, galleries, and cultural institutions accessible to residents. The economy is diverse and strong, with finance, professional services, creative industries, pharmaceuticals, and technology all significant sectors. London''s tech scene is rapidly growing, with thriving communities in fintech, biotech, and software development. The NHS provides universal healthcare to all residents. Infrastructure is excellent, with reliable public transportation and modern facilities. The cost of living, especially in London and Southeast England, is among Europe''s highest. Brexit has created regulatory changes affecting immigration and business operations that prospective residents and investors must navigate. English is the official language. The UK offers strong career prospects for skilled professionals, particularly in finance, technology, healthcare, and law. The country provides access to European markets and extensive international business networks. Weather is notoriously grey and rainy. UK offers unparalleled opportunities for ambitious professionals and access to world-class institutions, balanced by high living costs and post-Brexit regulatory considerations.'),
    ('Europe', 'Switzerland', 'CH', 'https://flagcdn.com/ch.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1527668752968-14dc70a27c95?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'A Swiss paradise nestled in the Alps known for precision, quality, and innovation. Switzerland offers exceptional standards of living, excellent healthcare, and world-class banking and pharmaceutical sectors.

## Key Highlights
- Exceptional standard of living and quality of life
- World-class healthcare and banking systems
- Strong economy in pharmaceuticals and innovation', 'Switzerland is a small Alpine nation renowned for precision engineering, quality manufacturing, banking, pharmaceutical innovation, and exceptional quality of life. The country is not an EU member but maintains close economic ties with Europe. Zurich and Geneva are major international financial centers, hosting global organizations including the UN and Red Cross. Switzerland consistently ranks among the world''s wealthiest nations with one of the highest standards of living. Healthcare is excellent and comprehensive, though expensive. The Swiss education system is highly regarded, offering apprenticeship programs alongside academic education. The landscape is stunning, with Alps, lakes, and charming towns offering year-round recreational opportunities. Precision engineering, pharmaceuticals, and luxury goods manufacturing remain economic mainstays. Zurich and Geneva host growing tech scenes and startup ecosystems. The cost of living is among the world''s highest, with housing particularly expensive. Salaries are correspondingly high, often 30-50% above comparable European positions. Switzerland has four national languages: German, French, Italian, and Romansh, varying by region. Immigration is strictly controlled, with preference for highly skilled workers. Renewable energy is a focus, with hydropower providing most electricity. Switzerland offers banking secrecy and favorable tax conditions for certain residents. The country is politically stable and safe. Switzerland represents peak European quality of life, opportunity, and security, though at exceptionally high costs and with immigration challenges.'),
    ('Europe', 'Italy', 'IT', 'https://flagcdn.com/it.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1529154036614-a60975f5c760?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'The birthplace of the Renaissance, Italy captivates with ancient ruins, world-renowned art, exquisite food, and picturesque landscapes. From Rome to Milan, opportunities abound in culture, fashion, and design.

## Key Highlights
- Birthplace of Renaissance with world-renowned art
- Exquisite cuisine and vibrant food culture
- Growing opportunities in fashion, design, and tourism', 'Italy is a Mediterranean nation with profound historical and cultural significance, home to the Roman Empire, Renaissance art, and continuous influence on Western civilization. Rome, the capital, contains thousands of years of history alongside modern city infrastructure. Italy''s art heritage is unparalleled, with masterpieces by Michelangelo, Leonardo da Vinci, Botticelli, and countless others. Italian cuisine is world-renowned and central to national identity, with regional specialties, excellent wines, and agricultural tradition. The country''s landscape ranges from northern Alps to Mediterranean coast, with charming hillside towns and picturesque countryside. Venice, Florence, and Milan are major cultural and economic centers. Milan is a fashion and design capital, hosting world-class design schools and companies. Italy''s economy has faced challenges but remains significant in Europe. The cost of living varies dramatically: major tourist cities and Milan are expensive, but Southern Italy and smaller towns remain affordable. Healthcare is good and publicly funded. Italian is the official language; English proficiency varies significantly. Immigration procedures are less streamlined than some countries. Italy offers exceptional cultural experiences, excellent cuisine, natural beauty, and art heritage. The country attracts expats, students, and retirees seeking Mediterranean living and cultural enrichment. Challenges include bureaucratic complexity, economic uncertainty, and regional inequality. Italy combines unmatched cultural heritage, exquisite lifestyle, natural beauty, and culinary excellence, making it profoundly attractive despite economic and bureaucratic challenges.'),
    ('Europe', 'Netherlands', 'NL', 'https://flagcdn.com/nl.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1534351590666-13e3e96b5017?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'A progressive and efficient nation known for its bicycles, windmills, and tulips. The Netherlands offers excellent work-life balance, outstanding infrastructure, and a welcoming expat community in Amsterdam.

## Key Highlights
- Excellent work-life balance and quality of life
- World-class infrastructure and public services
- Welcoming expat community with English-friendly culture', 'The Netherlands is a Western European nation known for efficiency, progressive values, and exceptional quality of life. Amsterdam, the capital, is a vibrant and international city with world-class museums, canals, cycling infrastructure, and a thriving cultural scene. The country is famously flat, crisscrossed by bicycle paths and canals, making cycling the primary transportation. Dutch people generally speak excellent English, making it accessible for foreign residents. The economy is highly developed and diverse, with strong sectors in finance, agriculture, manufacturing, and technology. The Netherlands ranks among the world''s most innovative economies. Healthcare is excellent and well-organized. The education system is highly regarded. The cost of living is moderate to high, particularly in Amsterdam and other major cities. Work-life balance is exceptional by international standards, with strong labor protections and emphasis on personal time. The Dutch are known for directness and egalitarian values. Public services and infrastructure are world-class. The country offers numerous visa options for skilled workers, entrepreneurs, and investors. The flat landscape and excellent cycling infrastructure promote outdoor recreation and a healthy lifestyle. Challenges include high housing costs in major cities and competition for accommodation. The Netherlands combines progressive values, efficiency, English-friendly environment, exceptional infrastructure, work-life balance, and cultural openness, making it highly attractive to international professionals and families.'),
    ('Europe', 'Ireland', 'IE', 'https://flagcdn.com/ie.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1590089415225-401ed6f9db8e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'The Emerald Isle combines Celtic heritage with modern tech hubs. Dublin is a major European tech center with a vibrant culture, while the countryside offers stunning natural beauty and a warm Irish welcome.

## Key Highlights
- Major European tech and startup hub
- Vibrant culture with warm and friendly locals
- Stunning natural beauty and Celtic heritage', 'Ireland is an island nation off the coast of Western Europe, known for its Celtic heritage, literary traditions, and increasingly prominent tech industry. Dublin, the capital, has transformed into a major European tech hub, hosting European headquarters for Facebook, Google, Apple, and other tech giants. Irish culture emphasizes storytelling, music, literature, and community bonds. The Irish are known for warmth, humor, and hospitality. The countryside is stunningly beautiful, with dramatic cliffs, green landscapes, misty mountains, and coastal regions. Irish literature and music have influenced world culture profoundly. The economy has grown significantly, driven by tech companies, pharmaceuticals, and financial services. Dublin''s startup ecosystem rivals other European capitals. Ireland is an English-speaking country, making it accessible to international workers. Healthcare is decent though sometimes challenging. The cost of living, particularly in Dublin, has risen significantly due to tech industry growth and strong economy. Irish tax policies are favorable for businesses, attracting corporate investment. The weather is typically cool, rainy, and grey. Public transportation in Dublin is adequate; outside the capital, a car is often necessary. Ireland offers competitive salaries in tech, a thriving cultural scene, natural beauty, and English-speaking environment. Challenges include high housing costs, weather, and Brexit effects on trade. Ireland combines tech opportunity, cultural richness, natural beauty, warm people, and English-language accessibility, making it attractive for tech professionals and those seeking Celtic heritage with modern innovation.'),
    ('Europe', 'Greece', 'GR', 'https://flagcdn.com/gr.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1533105079780-92b9be482077?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'Cradle of Western civilization, Greece offers ancient history, Mediterranean charm, and island living. With affordable costs, excellent cuisine, and a relaxed lifestyle, Greece attracts expats from around the world.

## Key Highlights
- Cradle of Western civilization with ancient history
- Affordable cost of living with Mediterranean lifestyle
- Beautiful islands and world-class cuisine', 'Greece is a Mediterranean nation with profound historical significance as the birthplace of Western democracy, philosophy, and classical civilization. Athens, the capital, is home to the Parthenon and thousands of ancient ruins that shaped Western thought. The country consists of mainland territories and numerous islands, each with distinct character and beauty. Greek islands like Santorini, Mykonos, and Crete are world-famous vacation destinations with white-washed buildings, blue domes, and Mediterranean culture. The cost of living is affordable compared to Northern Europe, particularly outside major tourist areas and Athens. Greek cuisine is Mediterranean excellence: fresh seafood, olives, feta cheese, and healthy cooking traditions. Wine production is ancient, with many regions producing excellent local varieties. The Greek lifestyle emphasizes community, family, and enjoying life''s pleasures. Healthcare is adequate and affordable. Greek is the official language; English proficiency varies. The economy has recovered from previous crises but remains moderately developed. Greece offers various residency programs for entrepreneurs, investors, and remote workers. Expats are attracted by affordability, Mediterranean beauty, island living, history, and relaxed lifestyle. Challenges include bureaucratic complexity, sometimes inconsistent services, and economic uncertainty. Greece combines ancient history, Mediterranean beauty, affordable living, excellent cuisine, island lifestyle, and cultural richness, making it attractive for retirees, digital nomads, and those seeking Mediterranean living with historical depth.'),
    ('Europe', 'Belgium', 'BE', 'https://flagcdn.com/be.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1491557345352-5929e343eb89?q=80&w=1170&auto=format&fit=crop&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxwaG90by1wYWdlfHx8fGVufDB8fHx8fA%3D%3D', 'The heart of Europe, Belgium is home to the EU headquarters and a perfect base for European exploration. Known for chocolate, beer, and medieval architecture, it offers urban sophistication in Brussels and Antwerp.

## Key Highlights
- Heart of Europe and EU headquarters
- Famous for world-class chocolate and Belgian beer
- Medieval architecture and urban sophistication', 'Belgium is a small Western European nation serving as the de facto capital of the European Union, with Brussels hosting EU headquarters and major international organizations. The country is strategically located, serving as a gateway to Europe for international business. Belgium is bilingual: French (Walloon) in the south and Dutch (Flemish) in the north, creating distinct regional cultures. Brussels is an international city with diverse communities and excellent international schools. The country is famous for Belgian chocolate, considered among the world''s finest, and Belgian beer with diverse styles and high quality. Medieval architecture is preserved in cities like Bruges and Ghent, offering picturesque charm. Belgium offers excellent infrastructure, public services, and quality of life. The education system is good, particularly regarding international schools. Healthcare is excellent and well-organized. The cost of living is moderate to high. Belgium offers opportunities in EU administration, international organizations, finance, and technology. Chocolate and beer industries provide niche opportunities. English is widely spoken in urban areas and international business contexts. Belgium''s small size makes it easy to travel to neighboring countries. Challenges include linguistic complexity, weather, and competition for jobs in major sectors. Belgium combines European strategic importance, international business hub status, culinary excellence, medieval charm, and excellent infrastructure, making it attractive for EU professionals, expats, and those seeking a European base.'),
    ('Europe', 'Poland', 'PL', 'https://flagcdn.com/pl.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1538332576228-eb5b4c4de6f5?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'A dynamic Central European nation with rich history and a booming economy. Poland offers affordable living costs, growing tech opportunities, and a vibrant cultural scene centered in Warsaw and Krakow.

## Key Highlights
- Affordable living costs with booming economy
- Growing tech and startup ecosystem
- Rich history and vibrant cultural scene', 'Poland is a Central European nation with a rich, complex history and increasingly dynamic modern economy. Warsaw, the capital, has been rebuilt multiple times and now represents modern Polish ambition with contemporary architecture alongside historical sites. Krakow is known for its preserved medieval old town, cultural heritage, and thriving arts scene. Poland''s economy is one of Europe''s fastest-growing, driven by manufacturing, IT, finance, and consumer services. The country has developed a significant tech sector, with Krakow and Warsaw hosting growing startup ecosystems. The cost of living is lower than Western Europe, making Poland attractive for remote workers and digital nomads. Polish cuisine is hearty and flavorful, with strong traditions. Polish people are generally friendly and welcoming to foreigners, though learning some Polish is appreciated. Healthcare is adequate and affordable. The education system is improving and university education is affordable. English proficiency is increasing among younger people and urban professionals. Poland offers various visa options for remote workers, entrepreneurs, and investors. The country combines European EU membership with affordability and opportunities. Challenges include language barriers outside major cities, visa bureaucracy, and stereotypes. Poland''s economy and opportunities are rapidly developing. Poland combines affordability, economic dynamism, tech opportunities, cultural richness, EU membership, and increasingly international character, making it attractive for those seeking Central European living with growth opportunities and low costs.'),
    ('Europe', 'Austria', 'AT', 'https://flagcdn.com/at.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1520503922584-590e8f7a90d7?q=80&w=1170&auto=format&fit=crop&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxwaG90by1wYWdlfHx8fGVufDB8fHx8fA%3D%3D', 'The home of classical music and imperial heritage, Austria offers elegance and culture in Vienna. Known for its high quality of life, pristine alpine scenery, and strong economy in engineering and technology.

## Key Highlights
- Home of classical music and imperial heritage
- High quality of life with pristine Alpine scenery
- Strong economy in engineering and technology', 'Austria is a Central European nation known for classical music, imperial history, and exceptional quality of life. Vienna, the capital, is a UNESCO World Heritage city renowned for music, architecture, museums, and coffee culture. Austria''s connection to Mozart, Beethoven, and other classical composers profoundly shaped Western music. The Austro-Hungarian imperial heritage remains visible in Vienna''s grand palaces, architecture, and cultural institutions. Austria combines Alpine natural beauty with urban culture. The economy is well-developed and diversified, with strengths in engineering, automotive, pharmaceuticals, and tourism. Austria offers excellent healthcare, education, and social services. The cost of living is moderate to high, particularly in Vienna. Work-life balance is valued, with strong labor protections. German is the official language; English is widely spoken in major cities and among younger professionals. Austria offers beautiful outdoor recreation: skiing, hiking, and mountain activities. Vienna is ranked among the world''s most livable cities. The country is culturally sophisticated with excellent museums, concert halls, and theaters. Austria offers visa options for skilled workers, entrepreneurs, and investors. Challenges include German language importance and competition for jobs. Austria combines cultural sophistication, classical heritage, Alpine beauty, exceptional quality of life, strong economy, and European stability, making it attractive for those valuing culture, nature, and quality of life.'),
    ('Asia', 'Turkey', 'TR', 'https://flagcdn.com/tr.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1527838832700-5059252407fa?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'Straddling Europe and Asia, Turkey blends ancient history with modern energy. Istanbul is a vibrant cultural hub, while the Aegean coast offers stunning beaches and affordable Mediterranean living.

## Key Highlights
- Bridge between Europe and Asia with rich history
- Vibrant Istanbul and Mediterranean beaches
- Affordable living with dynamic culture', 'Turkey is a transcontinental country straddling Europe and Asia, blending cultures, histories, and contemporary dynamism. Istanbul is a major international city hosting over 15 million people, spanning two continents across the Bosphorus Strait. The city is a cultural crossroads with stunning architecture, mosques, palaces, museums, and vibrant street life. Turkey''s history spans numerous civilizations: ancient Greeks, Romans, Byzantines, and Ottomans. Archaeological sites include Troy and Ephesus. The Turkish economy is one of Europe''s largest, diversified across manufacturing, services, agriculture, and tourism. The cost of living is affordable, particularly outside Istanbul and major tourist areas. Turkish cuisine is sophisticated and world-renowned, with regional specialties and kebab traditions. The Aegean and Mediterranean coasts offer beautiful beaches and vacation destinations. Turkish hospitality is legendary. Turkish is the official language; English proficiency varies by region and age. Healthcare is modern in major cities and more basic elsewhere. Turkey offers visa options for remote workers, investors, and retirees. Challenges include visa restrictions, political uncertainty, economic volatility, and currency fluctuations. Women travelers and residents should be aware of cultural differences. Turkey combines historical significance, cultural dynamism, affordability, geographical beauty, and Asian-European fusion, making it attractive for adventurous expats, budget travelers, and those seeking cultural immersion.'),
    ('Europe', 'Malta', 'MT', 'https://flagcdn.com/mt.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1587974928552-4f4aac51b45d?q=80&w=1506&auto=format&fit=crop&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxwaG90by1wYWdlfHx8fGVufDB8fHx8fA%3D%3D', 'A Mediterranean microstate with a thriving economy and excellent location. Malta offers EU membership, English-speaking communities, sunny weather, and growing opportunities in gaming and iGaming sectors.

## Key Highlights
- EU membership with English-speaking locals
- Year-round sunny weather and Mediterranean living
- Growing iGaming and fintech industries', 'Malta is a small Mediterranean island nation and EU member state strategically located between Europe and North Africa. Valletta, the capital, is a UNESCO World Heritage city with stunning architecture and harbor views. English is an official language alongside Maltese, making it highly accessible to English speakers. Malta enjoys Mediterranean climate with sunny weather year-round, attracting retirees and those seeking consistent sunshine. The economy is small but vibrant, with gaming, iGaming, and online gambling being significant industries. Financial services and tourism are also important sectors. Malta actively attracts tech entrepreneurs and remote workers. EU citizenship can be obtained through investment programs. The cost of living is moderate. Healthcare is good and publicly funded. Malta''s size (about 500,000 people) makes it intimate and easy to navigate. The country has low crime rates and is very safe. Malta offers incredible beaches and Mediterranean beauty. The iGaming and fintech sectors are thriving. Challenges include summer heat and tourist crowds, visa restrictions for non-EU citizens, and limited job market outside specific sectors. Malta combines Mediterranean charm, EU membership, English-language accessibility, safety, year-round sunshine, growing tech opportunities, and citizenship investment options, making it attractive for entrepreneurs, remote workers, retirees, and EU passport seekers.'),
    ('Europe', 'Denmark', 'DK', 'https://flagcdn.com/dk.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1513622470522-26c3c8a854bc?q=80&w=1170&auto=format&fit=crop&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxwaG90by1wYWdlfHx8fGVufDB8fHx8fA%3D%3D', 'A Scandinavian gem known for happiness and quality of life. Copenhagen is a progressive capital with excellent design, cycling culture, and strong job opportunities in tech and renewable energy.

## Key Highlights
- World''s happiest countries with high quality of life
- Progressive Copenhagen with excellent design culture
- Strong opportunities in tech and renewable energy', 'Denmark is a Scandinavian nation consistently ranked among the world''s happiest countries with exceptional quality of life. Copenhagen, the capital, is a progressive, vibrant city known for design culture, cycling infrastructure, and innovative restaurants. The city ranks among the world''s best for livability. Danes are known for their egalitarian values, work-life balance emphasis, and cycling culture. The economy is strong and diversified, with strengths in renewable energy, wind power, pharmaceuticals, and shipping. Denmark is a global leader in wind energy, with substantial windfarms supplying electricity. Copenhagen''s design schools are world-renowned, attracting creative professionals globally. The cost of living is among Europe''s highest, with Copenhagen particularly expensive. Healthcare is excellent and publicly funded. The education system is highly regarded. Danish people are reserved initially but warm once acquainted. Danish is the official language, though English is widely spoken. Work-life balance is exceptional, with emphasis on personal time and family. The weather is cool and grey much of the year. Cycling is the primary transportation in Copenhagen. Denmark offers visa options for skilled workers. Challenges include high costs, weather, and homogeneous society. Denmark combines happiness indices, exceptional quality of life, design culture, renewable energy leadership, progressive values, and work-life balance, making it attractive for those prioritizing well-being, design, sustainability, and Nordic lifestyle.'),
    ('Europe', 'Sweden', 'SE', 'https://flagcdn.com/se.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1638487246661-8a62aa593a16?q=80&w=1170&auto=format&fit=crop&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxwaG90by1wYWdlfHx8fGVufDB8fHx8fA%3D%3D', 'A Nordic leader in innovation and sustainability, Sweden boasts Stockholm''s beauty, cutting-edge tech companies, and exceptional work-life balance. Known for IKEA, Spotify, and progressive social values.

## Key Highlights
- Nordic leader in innovation and sustainability
- World-famous companies like IKEA and Spotify
- Exceptional work-life balance and social values', 'Sweden is a Nordic nation renowned for innovation, sustainability, and exceptional quality of life. Stockholm, the capital, is built on 14 islands and ranks among the world''s most beautiful capital cities. Sweden has produced world-famous companies: IKEA, Spotify, Volvo, Ericsson, and Minecraft creator Mojang. The tech sector is vibrant and global, with Stockholm''s startup ecosystem rivaling Silicon Valley in some metrics. Sweden is a world leader in renewable energy and sustainability, with environmental values deeply embedded in culture. Swedes value equality, individual rights, and work-life balance. The education system is highly regarded and tuition-free through university. Healthcare is excellent. Swedish design is world-renowned for simplicity and functionality. The cost of living is high, particularly in Stockholm. Swedish is the official language, though English is widely spoken. The weather features long, dark winters and bright summers. Outdoor activities are central to Swedish life: hiking, skiing, and swimming. The Swedish concept of ''lagom'' (balance and moderation) characterizes society. Sweden offers visas for skilled workers. Challenges include high costs, weather, and a somewhat reserved culture initially. Sweden combines technological innovation, sustainability leadership, design excellence, work-life balance, natural beauty, and progressive values, making it ideal for tech professionals, sustainability-focused individuals, and those valuing Nordic quality of life.'),
    ('Europe', 'Finland', 'FI', 'https://flagcdn.com/fi.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1531737212413-667205e1cda7?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'The land of a thousand lakes and Northern lights, Finland excels in education and technology. Helsinki is a modern, sustainable capital with innovative companies and excellent quality of life.

## Key Highlights
- Thousand lakes and magical Northern Lights
- World''s best education system and innovation
- Modern, sustainable capital with high quality of life', 'Finland is a Nordic nation known for its thousand lakes, vast forests, Northern Lights, and world-leading education system. Helsinki, the capital, is a modern, design-forward city with innovative architecture and vibrant culture. Finland consistently ranks among the world''s happiest countries and has the world''s best education system, with no standardized tests and emphasis on play-based learning. The tech industry is globally significant, with Nokia, Supercell, Remedy Games, and thousands of startups originating here. Finland''s education-to-innovation pipeline is renowned. The country is a world leader in renewable energy and environmental sustainability. Finnish design and architecture are celebrated globally. The cost of living is moderate to high, particularly in Helsinki. Finland offers excellent healthcare. The language is Finnish, quite distinct from other Nordic languages, though English is widely spoken. The country experiences extreme seasons: brief, bright summers and long, dark winters with Northern Lights opportunities. Sauna culture is central to Finnish life. Work-life balance is excellent. Snow, lakes, and forests provide outdoor recreation. Finland offers visas for skilled workers and entrepreneurs. Challenges include weather, cost of living, and a somewhat reserved culture. Finland combines educational excellence, tech innovation, Nordic quality of life, natural beauty, sustainability commitment, and unique culture, making it attractive for tech professionals, educators, and those seeking Nordic living.'),
    ('Europe', 'Norway', 'NO', 'https://flagcdn.com/no.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1600256698889-61ff2cd73cd8?q=80&w=1171&auto=format&fit=crop&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxwaG90by1wYWdlfHx8fGVufDB8fHx8fA%3D%3D', 'A Scandinavian paradise of fjords, mountains, and natural beauty. Norway offers one of the world''s highest standards of living, excellent salaries, and abundant opportunities in energy and technology sectors.

## Key Highlights
- Spectacular fjords and pristine natural beauty
- One of world''s highest standards of living
- Excellent salaries and strong economy', 'Norway is a Scandinavian nation renowned for spectacular natural scenery: dramatic fjords, snow-capped mountains, Northern Lights, and vast forests. Oslo, the capital, is a vibrant city with modern architecture, museums, and cultural institutions. Norway consistently ranks among the world''s highest in quality of life, with exceptional standards. The economy is strong and diversified, with oil wealth (sovereign wealth fund) enabling extensive public services. Salaries in Norway are among the world''s highest, though so is the cost of living. The Norwegian welfare state provides exceptional healthcare, education, and social benefits. Norway is not an EU member but has close relationships. Norwegian is the official language, though English is very widely spoken. Norwegians value outdoor recreation and nature connection; hiking, skiing, and outdoor sports are central. The country leads in renewable energy and sustainability. English proficiency is nearly universal among younger people and professionals. Work-life balance is excellent. The weather features long, dark winters and brief, bright summers. The cost of living is among the world''s highest. Immigration is selective, prioritizing skilled workers. Challenges include extreme costs, weather, and limited visa pathways. Norway combines natural beauty, exceptional quality of life, high salaries, Nordic values, outdoor lifestyle, and sustainability leadership, making it ideal for wealthy retirees, skilled workers, and those seeking Scandinavian living at any cost.'),
    ('Europe', 'Cyprus', 'CY', 'https://flagcdn.com/cy.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1677023484291-005b9840132f?q=80&w=1170&auto=format&fit=crop&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxwaG90by1wYWdlfHx8fGVufDB8fHx8fA%3D%3D', 'A Mediterranean island paradise with year-round sunshine, beautiful beaches, and a relaxed lifestyle. Cyprus offers EU citizenship, favorable tax benefits, and a growing expat community in Nicosia and Limassol.

## Key Highlights
- Year-round sunshine and Mediterranean beaches
- EU citizenship and favorable tax benefits
- Growing expat community and relaxed lifestyle', 'Cyprus is a Mediterranean island nation and EU member state offering year-round sunshine, stunning beaches, and relaxed Mediterranean lifestyle. The island has strategic geographic location between Europe, Asia, and Africa. The Republic of Cyprus is divided, with the northern part controlled by Northern Cyprus (recognized only by Turkey). Nicosia is the capital, while Limassol and Paphos are major tourist and expat hubs. Cyprus offers EU citizenship through property investment programs. The cost of living is moderate, with significant affordability outside main resort areas. Healthcare is good and affordable. Mediterranean climate with over 300 days of sunshine annually. Cyprus offers various visa programs and residency options for retirees, remote workers, and investors. The economy is based on tourism, shipping, and services. English is widely spoken due to tourism and expat communities. Beaches and Mediterranean culture attract retirees and those seeking warm climates. Expat communities are well-established, providing support networks. Tax benefits are available for certain residents. Challenges include political division, financial crisis history, and visa restrictions for some nationalities. Cyprus combines Mediterranean beauty, EU membership, citizenship investment opportunities, sunshine, beaches, affordability, and established expat communities, making it attractive for retirees, remote workers, and those seeking southern European island living.'),
    ('Europe', 'France', 'FR', 'https://flagcdn.com/fr.svg', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1499856871958-5b9627545d1a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80', 'The City of Light and much more, France captivates with art, wine, cuisine, and culture. From Paris to the Côte d''Azur, it offers timeless elegance, world-class museums, and a refined lifestyle.

## Key Highlights
- World-class art, museums, and cultural heritage
- Exquisite cuisine and wine traditions
- Timeless elegance and refined lifestyle', 'France is a Western European nation with profound cultural influence globally, known as the world''s most visited country. Paris, the capital, is often called the City of Light and is renowned for its beauty, art, architecture, romance, and influence. France is synonymous with art (Louvre Museum), fashion (haute couture), wine, cuisine, and refined culture. French gastronomy is UNESCO-recognized intangible cultural heritage. French wine regions produce world''s finest wines from Bordeaux, Burgundy, Champagne, and Provence. Paris offers unparalleled museums, galleries, theaters, and cultural institutions. The French Riviera (Côte d''Azur) is world-famous for beaches, towns like Monaco and Nice, and Mediterranean lifestyle. The economy is one of Europe''s largest and most diversified. The education system is well-developed. Healthcare is excellent. Cost of living is high in Paris, particularly for housing. French is the official language; English proficiency varies, being lower in France than many European countries. French culture emphasizes elegance, philosophy, and joie de vivre. The French value work-life balance and extended vacation time. The country is politically stable with strong institutions. Immigration requires sponsorship typically. Challenges include expensive Paris living, French language importance, and bureaucratic complexity. France combines unmatched cultural heritage, culinary excellence, artistic traditions, Mediterranean beauty, sophisticated lifestyle, and global influence, making it ideal for those valuing culture, art, wine, and refined living despite high costs.')
